{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533617-wi-baali-hecata","id":1533617,"title":"WI: Baali = Hecata","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-05T10:05:29-07:00","id":1533617,"title":"WI: Baali = Hecata","content":"I thought of a setting riff while on the thread about rewriting the Giovanni - what if the Hecata are the Baali.<br /> <br /> I don't just mean the new Clan called the Hecata, I mean going all the way back to the beginning. There never was a Cappadocian Clan, it was always the Baali.<br /> <br /> By most accounts, Ashur, the Antediluvian who spilled his blood into the pit of demon worshipers to create the Baali is the Cappadocian founder. This would already make the Baali a Cappadocian Bloodline. Though the Baali have been so active and prominent compared to the Cappadocians, they are the ones who should have been the full fledged Clan with Necromancy as their Discipline. A far more interesting and fittingly evil Discipline than Daimoinon is.<br /> <br /> The Baali has long had an interest in creepy inbred families, going back to the D'Habi, and this can be extended forward to the Giovanni, Rossellini, Dunsirn, etc.<br /> <br /> What about Cappadocius and the creation of the Giovanni? If one wanted to preserve the canon story relatively unchanged, then Cappadocius could be a Baali methuselah who abandoned the main Clan (perhaps he is Moloch) and Augustus Giovanni became 4th generation.<br /> <br /> I'm sure this idea could be fleshed out a bit more, but are there any initial thoughts (aside from saying that it sucks) or any suggestions about how to flesh this out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T10:57:39-07:00","id":1533620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533617-wi-baali-hecata#post1533617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By most accounts, Ashur, the Antediluvian who spilled his blood into the pit of demon worshipers to create the Baali is the Cappadocian founder. This would already make the Baali a Cappadocian Bloodline. Though the Baali have been so active and prominent compared to the Cappadocians, they are the ones who should have been the full fledged Clan with Necromancy as their Discipline. A far more interesting and fittingly evil Discipline than Daimoinon is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think &quot;by most accounts&quot; is incorrect, Saulot was the first name associated with the Baali founding, and I suspect if you count the mentions across all the editions his name would still be the most common. <br /> <br /> That said, I don't think it matters much, if you want to explore this in a game, go for it, no one can stop you. Personally I think I'd cleave a little closer to the original lore but perhaps play up how the Baali infiltrated the Cappadocious maybe it was they who engineered Augustus's diablerie of Cappadocious. Heck, perhaps they engineered Tremere's as well. You could do a lot with it without changing the whole clan. But as always, do whatever you think will make a good story. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T10:36:55-07:00","id":1533708,"title":"","content":"Myself I still like the idea of the Baali as a sect of infernals made up of numerous clan members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T11:07:07-07:00","id":1533710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533617-wi-baali-hecata?p=1533708#post1533708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Myself I still like the idea of the Baali as a sect of infernals made up of numerous clan members.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would be interesting as well. It would help explain how active and influential the Baali have been over the millennia. Especially when they have so many powerful enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T12:40:20-07:00","id":1533714,"title":"","content":"Making Mariah a Hecate would be a good answer to what clan she is in regards to either idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T13:22:59-07:00","id":1533716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533617-wi-baali-hecata?p=1533708#post1533708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Myself I still like the idea of the Baali as a sect of infernals made up of numerous clan members.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I view the Baali as well. In my chronicles they are a specific sect or cult of infernalists that have some sort of sorcerous rite they use as an initiation which pollutes their vitae, gives them an additional weakness (a Flaw), and grants them access to the Daimonen Discipline (which otherwise cannot be learned).<br /> <br /> I don't think the Dark Ages version of the Baali reflect anything like how they were supposed to be used so I find that gameline's canon to be troublesome, but there are lots of things I think can be used in my own interpretation. (I think that the Dark Ages game trying to treat the Setites like a normal clan, it basically gave the Baali the original role the Setites were to play in the setting.) I've never quite seen what unique angle the Baali really bring to the Vampire setting since it already has &quot;normal&quot; infernalists plus the Setites. So what makes yet a third group of evil demon worshippers different? Though the key thing for me is that given they were originally described as wanting to summon their masters back into this world to turn the planet into a demon-ridden hell that they have to be directly tied into the ending of the world and thus Gehenna. Thus they have an important eschatological role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T16:10:41-07:00","id":1533725,"title":"","content":"What about the conspiracy about Saulot being the progenitor of the Baali?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T16:22:51-07:00","id":1533726,"title":"","content":"You could use the notion of Saulot being the founder of the Baali as misinformation or propaganda to justify the blood hunt for his clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T18:51:38-07:00","id":1533731,"title":"","content":"Given how outliers like the Nagaraja slipped into the Hecata due to using necromancy I think having Baali infiltrating the clan's/sect's ranks is a fun idea I'm sure plenty of demon trickery could masquerade as necromancy. I'd def steal this for a chronicle subplot<br /> <br /> I'm also in the camp of the Baali being founded by the Salubri (for the irony) and poaching comrades from the more respectable clans when they aren't making the occasional mortal eat a vitae-laced heart in a slimy well, but the Shadowlands and the Abyss are close by so I could see how them being another Cappadocian bloodline checks out if thats anyone's personal canon. A misguided Graverobber who sought god but found the devil instead sounds like the type of antagonist good Baali tend to be","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28284-abugintherug","name":"abugintherug","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28284_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T21:30:11-07:00","id":1533733,"title":"","content":"You know Mariah could also work as a member of the Lasombra clan almost as well as a member of the Hecate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T19:21:08-07:00","id":1533783,"title":"","content":"Does her clan really matter any more? I thought she had ascended/descended into demonhood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T19:28:59-07:00","id":1533785,"title":"","content":"It sounds like in the revised version of Vampire The Masquerade is that they changed the details of Mariah history and now under the sway of Michael she is residing in Instanbul to recreate the dream. Besides this post is all about tweaking the Baali in the current setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T20:51:14-07:00","id":1533796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533617-wi-baali-hecata?p=1533716#post1533716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's how I view the Baali as well. In my chronicles they are a specific sect or cult of infernalists that have some sort of sorcerous rite they use as an initiation which pollutes their vitae, gives them an additional weakness (a Flaw), and grants them access to the Daimonen Discipline (which otherwise cannot be learned).<br /> <br /> I don't think the Dark Ages version of the Baali reflect anything like how they were supposed to be used so I find that gameline's canon to be troublesome, but there are lots of things I think can be used in my own interpretation. (I think that the Dark Ages game trying to treat the Setites like a normal clan, it basically gave the Baali the original role the Setites were to play in the setting.) I've never quite seen what unique angle the Baali really bring to the Vampire setting since it already has &quot;normal&quot; infernalists plus the Setites. So what makes yet a third group of evil demon worshippers different? Though the key thing for me is that given they were originally described as wanting to summon their masters back into this world to turn the planet into a demon-ridden hell that they have to be directly tied into the ending of the world and thus Gehenna. Thus they have an important eschatological role.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for me the Setites, first and foremost, are Antedeluvian worshippers, not demon worshippers. They worship their clan founder (and note that you don't really have Antedeluvian worshippers as a general thing outside of the True Black Hand). Granted there are Gehenna cults, but those were barely ever explored. Then the Baali are more of an organized group of demon worshippers (rather than a small infernalist clubs or independent infernalists like you normally see) which sets the Baali up better to be used as a large-scale conspiracy that can cross between sects and draw on resources that smaller infernalist groups wouldn't be able to get. So I kind of feel like all 3 groups (Antedeluvian worshippers, Baali and independent infernalists) all have a place in the setting, <br /> <br /> I do tend to play up the idea that roughly half of Baali are inductees originally from other Clans, and in general the Baali don't really make a distinction between those who were sired by a Baali and those who were recruited (though there are some exceptions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T07:28:41-07:00","id":1533813,"title":"","content":"Anything is better than the &quot;Saulot founded the Baali&quot; bullshit. Like, obviously you have to make Saulot make the most IVOL Clan/Bloodline/Cult... i really prefer the idea of Ashur = Cappadocian, or that there are more than 13 Antes and the Baali just have their own Antediluvian","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28021-camaradadoppio","name":"CamaradaDoppio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28021_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T08:07:09-07:00","id":1533816,"title":"","content":"I think it works if you view the source of Necromancy, Infernalism, and Eldritch Powers to ultimately be the same one - kind of what the Oblivion Discipline already does for the Hecata, so I don't see a lot of trouble folding the Baali in as well in that case. It would have the advantage of streamlining the different brands and flavors of 'dark powers' that have accumulated throughout the versions.<br /> <br /> I personally don't see it that way and already had issues with Oblivion combining Necromancy and Obtenebration, because those are different sourced things for me. The Baali go even further with their internal split in three factions that want and do very different things. That said, the Baali as a Children of Osiris type construct who recruit (or re-embrace) more than they embrace isn't something I would mind at all, it would even be in line with their murky origin history.<br /> <br /> But without the distinction between Nergali, Molochim, and Unnamed that the Clanbook introduced, the Baali revert back to their original cast as pretty two-dimensional Infernalists, in which case I would have to agree that they kind of feel superfluous. Which is already an issue I had with the Hecata as a Clan, because some parts feel like they lost their identity and purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T22:08:37-07:00","id":1536924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533617-wi-baali-hecata#post1533617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought of a setting riff while on the thread about rewriting the Giovanni - what if the Hecata are the Baali.<br /> <br /> I don't just mean the new Clan called the Hecata, I mean going all the way back to the beginning. There never was a Cappadocian Clan, it was always the Baali.<br /> <br /> By most accounts, Ashur, the Antediluvian who spilled his blood into the pit of demon worshipers to create the Baali is the Cappadocian founder. This would already make the Baali a Cappadocian Bloodline. Though the Baali have been so active and prominent compared to the Cappadocians, they are the ones who should have been the full fledged Clan with Necromancy as their Discipline. A far more interesting and fittingly evil Discipline than Daimoinon is.<br /> <br /> The Baali has long had an interest in creepy inbred families, going back to the D'Habi, and this can be extended forward to the Giovanni, Rossellini, Dunsirn, etc.<br /> <br /> What about Cappadocius and the creation of the Giovanni? If one wanted to preserve the canon story relatively unchanged, then Cappadocius could be a Baali methuselah who abandoned the main Clan (perhaps he is Moloch) and Augustus Giovanni became 4th generation.<br /> <br /> I'm sure this idea could be fleshed out a bit more, but are there any initial thoughts (aside from saying that it sucks) or any suggestions about how to flesh this out?</div> </div> </div> </div>It always appeared to me that Saulot was the progenitor in the published works. But that doesn't matter. You can make it whoever you want it to be. This is fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T22:09:48-07:00","id":1536925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533617-wi-baali-hecata?p=1533708#post1533708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Myself I still like the idea of the Baali as a sect of infernals made up of numerous clan members.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, later it is as you claim. The Apostate ritual converts other clans to Baali.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T22:15:06-07:00","id":1536926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533617-wi-baali-hecata?p=1533716#post1533716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's how I view the Baali as well. In my chronicles they are a specific sect or cult of infernalists that have some sort of sorcerous rite they use as an initiation which pollutes their vitae, gives them an additional weakness (a Flaw), and grants them access to the Daimonen Discipline (which otherwise cannot be learned).<br /> <br /> I don't think the Dark Ages version of the Baali reflect anything like how they were supposed to be used so I find that gameline's canon to be troublesome, but there are lots of things I think can be used in my own interpretation. (I think that the Dark Ages game trying to treat the Setites like a normal clan, it basically gave the Baali the original role the Setites were to play in the setting.) I've never quite seen what unique angle the Baali really bring to the Vampire setting since it already has &quot;normal&quot; infernalists plus the Setites. So what makes yet a third group of evil demon worshippers different? Though the key thing for me is that given they were originally described as wanting to summon their masters back into this world to turn the planet into a demon-ridden hell that they have to be directly tied into the ending of the world and thus Gehenna. Thus they have an important eschatological role.</div> </div> </div> </div>According the the &quot;Metaplot,&quot; there are 2 official factions, and 1 left ambiguous. Nergal, who wants to summon the Infernal into the physical realm. Moloch, who wants to keep the Infernal appeased through sacrifices, while enjoying their endowments. And the &quot;Unnamed,&quot; who who is heavily implied to be Ur-Shulgi, whose ambitions are left unknown intentionally, to give Game Masters room to improvise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T22:20:30-07:00","id":1536927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533617-wi-baali-hecata?p=1533785#post1533785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like in the revised version of Vampire The Masquerade is that they changed the details of Mariah history and now under the sway of Michael she is residing in Instanbul to recreate the dream. Besides this post is all about tweaking the Baali in the current setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That retcon always bothered me. Ma-Ri-Ah being possessed by Mi-Ka-Il (the bad writing is painful) doesn't make sense in that she's become an ascended demon, and Michael isn't &quot;evil&quot; by Kindred standards, but he's just &quot;buying his time and observing&quot; to what I assume to be disemboweling infants into an organ pit, or worse atrocities.<br /> <br /> There's a reason White Wolf made Requiem to solve this bullshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T12:12:06-07:00","id":1537017,"title":"","content":"Remember Michael has been going mad for several centuries before being consumed by his former lover and you know that there essences are getting merged with one another and neither are the same person anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}